message: "If you use this tool in published research, please cite it as below."
title: "fair-maturity-copilot: A guided, plain-language FAIR data-maturity assessment tool"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Mugume Twinamatsiko"
    family-names: "Atwine"
    affiliation: "Africa Center of Excellence in Bioinformatics & Data Science (ACE), Kampala, Uganda"
repository-code: "https://github.com/atwine/fair-maturity-copilot"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-27"
keywords:
  - FAIR
  - data maturity
  - research data management
  - FAIR Data Maturity Model
  - RDA
  - data harmonization
  - multi-site data
abstract: >-
  A guided, plain-language FAIR data-maturity assessment tool for research
  organizations that don't have a data librarian on staff. Walks a
  non-technical stakeholder through a 12-indicator subset of the RDA FAIR
  Data Maturity Model in plain language, scores it, uses an LLM to turn
  every weak indicator into a specific actionable next step, and synthesizes
  the whole set of gaps into one ordered FAIRification plan. A second
  adapter (harmonization-v0) assesses whether multiple sites in one
  initiative describe their data consistently enough to combine and compare.
